<!-- ========== INTRO ========== -->
<section id="intro">
  <h1>Carbon Check</h1>
  <p class="lede">Chapter 3 is the longest chapter of the quarter and it hides seven separate ideas inside one word, carbon. Twenty-one questions sort out which of the seven you already own and which one is costing you the others. About eighteen minutes.</p>
  <p class="fine">Nothing is submitted. No score leaves this iPad and I never see it. Answer honestly and the result is worth something.</p>

  <div class="grid" id="introGrid"></div>

  <p class="fine" style="margin-bottom:1.6rem">Three questions on each idea. The colours are the ones used on the board for carbohydrates, lipids, proteins and nucleic acids, so a tile here and a diagram in class point at the same thing.</p>
  <button class="go" id="start">Start the check</button>
</section>

<!-- ========== QUESTION ========== -->
<section id="quiz" class="hidden">
  <div class="bar"><i id="fill" style="width:0%"></i></div>
  <div class="meta"><span id="bandName"></span><span id="counter"></span></div>
  <p class="q" id="stem"></p>
  <div class="opts" id="opts"></div>
  <div class="why hidden" id="why"><span class="tag" id="whyTag"></span><p id="whyText"></p></div>
  <button class="go hidden" id="next">Next</button>
</section>

<!-- ========== RESULTS ========== -->
<section id="results" class="hidden">
  <h1>Seven ideas, scored</h1>
  <p class="lede" id="summary"></p>
  <div class="grid" id="resultGrid"></div>
  <p class="fine">A heavy outline marks an idea to spend real time on. A filled tile is one you can trust and skip.</p>
  <h2>Work these, in this order</h2>
  <div id="bands"></div>
  <h2>Prove it on the Checkpoint</h2>
  <p>Checkpoint Chapter 3 sits on the NOVA Canvas Quizzes tab. Unlimited attempts, highest score kept, and it shows the right answer after every try. Take it cold, work the tasks above, take it again. Several of its questions put a numbered figure of six molecules in front of you and ask which one carries a particular group, so practise naming groups off a drawing rather than off a list.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:1.8rem"><button class="ghost" id="again">Run the check again</button></p>
</section>


